  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2024) position, SOLO basis, primarily from the bank's own audited Balance Sheet, Profit and Loss Account and the 'Highlights on the overall activities of the bank' annexure in that year's own annual report. FY2024 is the sector-wide asset-quality recognition year for this bank: classified loans jumped 178% (5,149,565,968 to 14,332,622,928), NPL ratio jumped from 5.93% to 16.17%, and a large provision deficit (Surplus/(deficit) provision against loans and advances = -6,558,390,257, i.e. a Tk.6.56bn shortfall) is reported directly in this year's own Annexure table -- against total shareholders' equity of only 11,045,530,488, this shortfall equals 59.4% of equity. PAT collapsed 79.7% (536,611,584 to 108,727,037) and ROE fell to 0.98% from 4.89% despite CRAR barely moving (13.80% vs 13.71%), i.e. capital ratios did not yet reflect the asset-quality deterioration. The FY2025 report's comparative column for FY2024 shows small reclassifications: total shareholders' equity restated to 11,075,579,274 (+30,048,786, +0.27%, mostly a new 'Start-up Equity Investment fund' equity line and a P&L-surplus/translation-reserve shuffle) and PAT restated to 112,406,475 (+3,679,438, +3.4% of a very small base, driven by a small increase in total operating income and a small decrease in total provision) -- both immaterial in absolute terms; this dataset keeps FY2024's own contemporaneous figures. Total Capital and CRAR directly reported and reconcile (11,769.90/85,274.64=13.803%=13.80%). Tier-I/Tier-II split specific to Solo not found in extractable text (only Consolidated-basis CET1=12.82%-of-13.75%-total); left as a gap.",
